<title>USA: USA-STOCKS-OUTLOOK.</title>
<headline>USA-STOCKS-OUTLOOK.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street stocks were seen opening higher on Friday after the Producer Price index registered a deeper-than-expected 0.4 percent decline in February, analysts said.</p>
<p>Jim Solloway, Director of Research at Argus Research, said: &quot;We should see a rebound in bond prices and that should help stocks ... numbers were weaker than expected.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;But current inflation hasn't been the problem, fear of future inflation has been the problem.&quot;</p>
</text>
